[38;2;124;124;124mlemma is:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor a $k$-form $\omega$ (here $k=1$, a vector field), define[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$(H\omega)(x) = \int_0^1 t^{k-1} \omega(tx) \cdot x \, dt$$ [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfor $k$-forms... let me recall the exact formula.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe Poincaré homotopy: Let $\omega$ be a $k$-form. The operator $I$ (integration[0m[38;2;124;124;124malong the homotopy from identity to zero map) gives a $(k-1)$-form:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m$$(I\omega)(x) = \int_0^1 t^{k-1} \iota_{\partial_t} \omega(tx) \, dt$$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mwhere $\iota$ is interior product... Actually let me just think in vector [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcalculus terms.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mFor a vector field $f$ (1-form), the potential is:[0m
