[38;2;124;124;124mUsing $\partial_j g_k = \partial_k g_j$ (curl-free): $= \int_0^1 g_j(tx)\,dt + [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\int_0^1 t\sum_k x_k \partial_k g_j(tx)\,dt$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet $h(t) = g_j(tx)$, so $h'(t) = \sum_k x_k \partial_k g_j(tx)$. Then:[0m

